#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cardinal-wake — owner-woken sessions (Claude Code adapter).

Run it in your own terminal (not through the agent):
    cardinal-wake enable              install the per-user launchd agent (macOS)
    cardinal-wake disable             remove it
    cardinal-wake status              the setting, recent notifications, candidate sessions and their
                                      resume commands
    cardinal-wake run [--once] [--dry-run]
    cardinal-wake resume <session> [--print]
                                      resume a session in this terminal (a unique 8+ hex prefix is enough)

When you post an owner decision on an Investigation page addressed to one
of your sessions, the waker shows a macOS notification (never the
decision's text). For a stopped session it names
`~/.cardinal/wake/lib/cardinal-wake resume <session>`; with terminal-notifier
installed, clicking it opens Terminal and runs that. `resume` runs the
session's own runtime resume in its recorded working directory, with the
decision as the first prompt:
    claude --resume <session> "<wake prompt>"
    codex resume <session> "<wake prompt>"   (a Codex desktop session opens in the app)
    gemini --resume <session> "<wake prompt>"
    cursor-agent --resume <session> "<wake prompt>"   (experimental)
For a session that is still open it says to switch to that window. Nothing
is ever launched unattended.

To answer a Claude Code session that is still running from another
device, start it with `claude --remote-control`.

The waker reads the investigation events with the Cardinal key of the
plugin whose session it is (this plugin's: CARDINAL_MCP_URL / CARDINAL_MCP_API_KEY in
~/.claude/settings.json `env`; nothing after /cardinal:disconnect). `enable` copies this plugin's
cardinal_core and a small runner into ~/.cardinal/wake/lib/ (re-copied by
every enable), so launchd and a notification's click never point into a
versioned plugin directory. The implementation is
cardinal_core.session_wake; see docs/specs/resume-and-wake.md §5.
"""

import sys
from pathlib import Path

PLUGIN_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(PLUGIN_ROOT / "hooks"))
from cardinal_core import session_wake  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(session_wake.cli_main(sys.argv[1:], runtime="claude", plugin_root=PLUGIN_ROOT))
